 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "make/do · heavy/strong · 형용사+명사 · 동사+명사",
   "en": "make and do · heavy and strong · adjective + noun · verb + noun"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "연어(collocation)는 자연스럽게 함께 쓰이는 단어 조합입니다. 같은 뜻이라도 짝이 정해져 있어서 한국어 직역으로는 틀리기 쉽습니다. make는 결과물을 만들거나 선택·소리를 나타내는 명사와 함께 쓰입니다(make a decision, make progress, make an effort, make a mistake). do는 일, 활동, 의무에 쓰입니다(do homework, do the housework, do business). 형용사와 명사의 짝도 정해져 있습니다(heavy traffic, strong wind, heavy rain, strong coffee). 단어를 외울 때 짝과 함께 외워 두면 유창성이 높아집니다.",
   "en": "Collocations are word combinations that sound natural together. Even with the same meaning the partner is fixed, so literal translation often goes wrong. Make is used for creating things, choices and sounds (make a decision, make progress, make an effort, make a mistake). Do is used for tasks, activities and duties (do homework, do the housework, do business). Adjective + noun pairs are also fixed (heavy traffic, strong wind, heavy rain, strong coffee). Learn words together with their partners to sound fluent."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "동사 / Verb",
    "짝 / Collocates",
    "예문 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "make",
     "a decision · progress · an effort",
     "I made a decision."
    ],
    [
     "do",
     "homework · the housework · business",
     "I do homework daily."
    ],
    [
     "heavy / strong",
     "traffic · rain / wind · coffee",
     "There was heavy traffic."
    ],
    [
     "keep / miss",
     "a promise · a secret / an opportunity",
     "He kept his promise."
    ]
   ]
  },
